rol she had her  passport  her butt Border Patrol said the picture  on the passport doesn't really look like  her she was questioned at nine years old  without her parents present when Border  Patrol was asked why did it take 32  hours to confirm her legal status as an  American citizen so far as of an hour  ago  Border Patrol has not had an explanation  Border Patrol tried to have Julia's 14  year old brother sign a document which  said actually julia is his cousin not  his sister insinuating some kind of  human trafficking angle to the entire  fiasco which of course is untrue it was  indeed his sister Border Patrol also  said Julia provided inconsistent  information during her questioning she's  nine years old did she first say Pete  says her favorite food and later said  that it's hotdogs she's nine years old  being questioned by law enforcement  without her parents eventually Julia's  mother was able to get the help of the  Mexican Consulate who contacted American  immigration authorities so I'm not  telling you this story to suggest that  this would be okay if Julia really  wasn't a citizen right this is a moral  crisis of the highest level no matter  what the nationality of the kids that  are being detained is what I'm trying to  point out to you is that first of all of  course this is hugely racially tinged  she's American with a passport but she's  non-white Hispanic crossing the border  from Mexico secondly if you're angry  about how she was treated realize that  it's just as bad for a nine-year-old  without an American passport to be  treated this way it's really easy for us  to sit back and not react strongly when  we're told listen a lot of these kids in  cages and kids being detained and  questioned by law enforcement with no  lawyers or parents a lot of them are  here illegally they're not American  citizens these are children  these are children they're not deciding  things for themselves if you are  horrified by this story of the  nine-year-old US ci